  {
   "id": 233102,
   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "<figure class=\"unnumbered\">\n<img src=\"exercises/media/07e45851ca913e1e.jpg\" alt=\"\">\n<figcaption>(credit: modification of work by Alexander M Makhov/ResearchGate)</figcaption>\n</figure>\n",
   "stem_html": "<p>The image shows electron microscope images of the DNA replication process. The strings in the image are DNA strands. The blob-like shapes are enzymes. The two DNA strands marked with arrows are single, not double. The enzymes are splitting the DNA into two strands.</p>\n<p>Based on this information, what type of enzyme is seen here?</p>",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 722553,
     "content_html": "DNA polymerase."
    },
    {
     "id": 722554,
     "content_html": "Helicase."
    },
    {
     "id": 722552,
     "content_html": "DNA ligase."
    },
    {
     "id": 722551,
     "content_html": "Topoisomerase."
    }
   ],
